3871- - COORDINATED RESOLUTION: Candidate release-builder notices, deterministic SPDX, provenance, 15/15 reproducibility, normalized archive, and four native rows now precede repository mutation. One isolated staged boundary then rotates the two source contracts, validator constants, Makefile and asset-tool archive defaults, Swift acceptance assertions, and generated inventory/provenance/notices/catalog/bundle as an exact ten-file tracked patch. A deliberately changed `0.0.0` / `e8bd954a…` candidate proved generation, audit, 21 supply-chain tests, 26 asset-manifest tests, four Swift catalog tests, and bundle checking without changing the accepted source tree; the initial red Swift run exposed and added the missing assertion surface rather than bypassing it.
3872- - FRESH-CLONE ANOMALY / FIX: A rework 02 reviewer found the deterministic audit stopped before building because a genuine clone does not contain the ignored `.temp` directory required by its `mktemp` template. Every `.temp`-backed `mktemp` boundary now creates that parent explicitly; the two `.build`-backed boundaries already create their immediate parents. A fresh `--no-local --no-hardlinks` clone with no pre-existing `.temp` then passed exact 15/15 comparison, native Darwin arm64 17/17, unsupported-runtime rejection before start, and the coordinated 10/10 rotation.
3873:+- DEFAULT-BUNDLE ANOMALY / FIX: A fresh clone with no pre-generated default trusted bundle exposed a relative-parent publication mismatch in the documented `make relay-asset-bundle-generate` invocation. The historical flow now passes the repository-absolute `.build/relay/relay-assets-v1` destination to both generation and checking. A fresh `--no-local --no-hardlinks` clone rebuilt both four-target archives at SHA-256 `1f0ba226ed591d1baf5f9464b33e45b7658a33bf5a1a114e77b6d22d3d9eef4e`, generated and checked the default bundle from an absent destination, and matched its trusted manifest byte-for-byte to the independently rebuilt historical manifest.
